{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ascending chain condition ascending chain condition","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md","fileName":"Ascending Chain Condition.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ascending Chain Condition","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Noetherian Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ascending chain condition ascending chain condition","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md","fileName":"Ascending Chain Condition.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Ascending Chain Condition","heading":"Ascending Chain Condition","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The ascending chain condition says that every increasing sequence of subobjects eventually stops changing. For ideals, a chain I₁ ⊆ I₂ ⊆ ··· is stationary when some stage equals every later stage.\n\nA ring satisfies this condition on ideals exactly when it is a [[Noetherian Ring]]. A module satisfying it on submodules is called Noetherian, linking chain behavior to finite generation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Noetherian Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Ascending Chain Condition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName